WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.854
Possible visual warning signs include inconsistent lighting or shadows,

00:00:03.854 --> 00:00:07.608
unnatural facial motion, unstable boundaries, repeated textures, implausible reflections,

00:00:07.608 --> 00:00:11.779
distorted hands or objects, and text that changes across frames.

00:00:11.779 --> 00:00:16.367
Audio clues may include odd cadence, abrupt tone changes, room-sound mismatch,

00:00:16.367 --> 00:00:17.618
or lip-sync problems.

00:00:17.618 --> 00:00:22.623
Background details deserve attention because generation and compositing may struggle with continuity.

00:00:22.623 --> 00:00:26.794
Signs, jewelry, clothing, furniture, and bystanders may transform across frames.

00:00:26.794 --> 00:00:29.296
However, motion blur, low bitrate, stabilization,

00:00:29.296 --> 00:00:32.216
and ordinary editing can produce similar effects.

00:00:32.216 --> 00:00:35.136
Compression artifacts are especially easy to misread.

00:00:35.136 --> 00:00:40.141
Social platforms resize and recompress media, destroying detail and creating blocks, ringing,

00:00:40.141 --> 00:00:40.975
or smearing.

00:00:40.975 --> 00:00:46.397
Multiple reposts make artifacts worse and can remove metadata that might otherwise help.

00:00:46.397 --> 00:00:48.900
Warning signs are leads, not proof.

00:00:48.900 --> 00:00:53.905
A single strange frame may result from network loss, interpolation, camera processing,

00:00:53.905 --> 00:00:55.573
or a paused expression.

00:00:55.573 --> 00:01:00.161
Genuine media can look artificial, and synthetic media can look natural.

00:01:00.161 --> 00:01:06.000
Examine patterns across multiple frames or audio segments and compare them with source context.

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:11.840
Preserve the original available file rather than relying on a screenshot of a repost.

00:01:11.840 --> 00:01:15.176
Document what was observed and plausible non-synthetic explanations.

00:01:15.176 --> 00:01:18.930
Do not declare authenticity because no artifact is visible.

00:01:18.930 --> 00:01:21.850
High-quality synthetic content may be technically convincing.

00:01:21.850 --> 00:01:27.272
Conversely, do not accuse a person or publisher because an image looks odd.

00:01:27.272 --> 00:01:31.860
Strong conclusions require provenance, corroboration, and a transparent chain of evidence.
